            "datePublished": "20 Jun 2025 03:39:13 GMT",
            "about": "Music for waiting, being held in a lukewarm limbo, listening for any activity on the line, and waiting some more. A soporific sense of unresolved tenuousness, a machine that loops indefinitely whether someone is listening or not.\nRecorded 24th October 2023 using the Moog Subharmonicon polyrhythmic analog synthesizer, the Strymon Magneto four-head tape delay system and the Multi Versio FX processor from Noise Engineering, with post-proc completed using the MSC Remote Array sometime in early 2025.",
            "credits": "released June 20, 2025\nW/P by Brian Grainger. Recorded at White Pillar Workshop, 24th October 2023 using the Moog Subharmonicon in conjunction with the Audioholistics modular system and the MSC Remote Array. Mastered by The Analog Botanist. Text by Brian. Design by ABM&D with the CLE and MR-10B palette. This is Milieu Music number PNH-10. (C) + (P) Oscillog ASCAP 2025. All nights preserved.",
